Names that need quoting, a space and a double quote in them: the plan
quotes every name it writes, its own double quotes doubled.

== before
CREATE TABLE "dish of the day" (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, "chef's ""pick""" TEXT) STRICT;
INSERT INTO "dish of the day" VALUES (1, 'soup');

== after
CREATE TABLE "dish of the day" (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, "chef's ""pick""" TEXT, note TEXT) STRICT;

== plan
roux: migrating test.db, 4 steps
  table `dish of the day`: aside, to make it anew
    ALTER TABLE "dish of the day" RENAME TO "roux_old_dish of the day"
  table `dish of the day`: as schema.sql makes it
    CREATE TABLE "dish of the day" (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, "chef's ""pick""" TEXT, note TEXT) STRICT
  table `dish of the day`: its rows, by id, chef's "pick"
    INSERT INTO "dish of the day" ("id", "chef's ""pick""") SELECT "id", "chef's ""pick""" FROM "roux_old_dish of the day"
  table `dish of the day`: the old one
    DROP TABLE "roux_old_dish of the day"
